%N A398721 Number of increasing 3-term arithmetic progressions in an n^4 hypercube.
%C A398721 The sequence counts how many increasing arithmetic progressions of three terms exist in a 4-dimensional hypercube. To provide context, each term in the arithmetic progressions is a four-dimensional coordinate vector. The vectors are compared lexicographically.
%H A398721 Hiller Alves Fernandes, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/21722745">Counting 3-Term Arithmetic Progressions in Integer Hypercubes</a>, Zenodo, (2026).
%F A398721 a(n) = ((x^2 + y^2)^4 - n^4)/2, where x = floor(n/2) and y = ceiling(n/2).
%o A398721 (Python)
%o A398721 def a(n, d=4): return (((n // 2)**2 + ((n + 1) // 2)**2)**d - n**d) // 2
%o A398721 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 28)])
%Y A398721 Column 4 of A397600.
